# 16. Incident Fix – Namespace Stuck in Terminating

### Problem

The error was:

```text
managedclusteraddons.addon.open-cluster-management.io
"governance-policy-framework" is forbidden:
unable to create new content in namespace ocm-cluster1
because it is being terminated
```

The root cause was:

```text
ocm-cluster1 namespace = Terminating
```

The namespace contained resources with OCM cleanup finalizers, including:

```text
manifestwork
rolebinding
```

and:

```text
cluster.open-cluster-management.io/manifest-work-cleanup
```

---

# 17. Diagnose a Terminating Managed-Cluster Namespace

Check:

```bash
kubectl get ns "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" -o yaml
```

Look for:

```yaml
deletionTimestamp:
phase: Terminating
```

Check remaining namespaced resources:

```bash
kubectl api-resources --verbs=list --namespaced -o name | while read r; do
  kubectl get "$r" \
    -n "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
    --ignore-not-found \
    -o name 2>/dev/null
done
```

Check ManifestWorks:

```bash
kubectl get manifestwork \
  -n "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}"
```

Check ManagedClusterAddOns:

```bash
kubectl get managedclusteraddon \
  -n "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}"
```

Check the ManagedCluster:

```bash
kubectl get managedcluster \
  "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
  -o jsonpath='deletionTimestamp={.metadata.deletionTimestamp}{"\n"}finalizers={.metadata.finalizers}{"\n"}'
```

