# 18. Correct Recovery Procedure

If the managed cluster is intentionally being removed, allow OCM's cleanup process to complete.

The correct cleanup order is:

```text
ManagedClusterAddOn
        ↓
ManifestWork
        ↓
cluster namespace cleanup
        ↓
namespace deletion completes
```

OCM specifically documents that `ManagedClusterAddOns` are deleted first, followed by `ManifestWorks`, to avoid resources being stuck in a terminating namespace.

Therefore:

### DO NOT immediately force-delete the namespace.

First allow OCM cleanup to finish.

Monitor:

```bash
kubectl get ns "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" -w
```

When cleanup is complete, the namespace should disappear:

```text
Error from server (NotFound):
namespaces "ocm-cluster1" not found
```

At that point the old cluster registration is completely removed.

---

# 19. Re-register the Managed Cluster After Cleanup

Once:

```bash
kubectl get ns "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}"
```

returns:

```text
NotFound
```

perform the normal registration again:

```bash
clusteradm join \
  --hub-token <TOKEN> \
  --hub-apiserver https://192.168.2.10:6443 \
  --wait \
  --cluster-name "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
  --context "${CTX_MANAGED_CLUSTER}"
```

Then accept on the hub:

```bash
clusteradm accept \
  --clusters "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"
```

Wait until:

```bash
kubectl get managedcluster \
  "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"
```

shows:

```text
HUB ACCEPTED   JOINED   AVAILABLE
true           True     True
```

---

# 20. Re-enable the Policy Add-ons

After the namespace is Active again:

```bash
kubectl get ns "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}"
```

Expected:

```text
Active
```

Enable:

```bash
clusteradm addon enable \
  --names governance-policy-framework \
  --clusters "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"
```

and:

```bash
clusteradm addon enable \
  --names config-policy-controller \
  --clusters "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"
```

Then verify:

```bash
kubectl get managedclusteraddon \
  -n "${MANAGED_CLUSTER_NAME}" \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"
```

