# 22. Final Expected Architecture

```text
                    OCM HUB
        ┌─────────────────────────────┐
        │ open-cluster-management     │
        │                             │
        │ ClusterManager              │
        │ Addon Manager               │
        │ Policy Propagator           │
        │ Governance Policy Controller│
        └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                       │
                       │ OCM registration
                       │ + ManifestWork
                       ▼
              ┌────────────────────┐
              │   ocm-cluster1     │
              │   Managed Cluster  │
              │                    │
              │ Klusterlet         │
              │ Work Agent         │
              │ Registration Agent │
              │                    │
              │ Policy Add-ons     │
              │ ├─ config-policy   │
              │ └─ governance      │
              └────────────────────┘
                       │
                       ▼
              Kubernetes resources
              / ClusterRoles
              / ConfigurationPolicy
              / other policies
```

# 23. Most Important Commands – Quick Reference

```bash
# Check clusteradm
clusteradm version

# Initialize hub
clusteradm init --wait --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Get managed-cluster join command
clusteradm get token --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Join managed cluster
clusteradm join \
  --hub-token <TOKEN> \
  --hub-apiserver https://192.168.2.10:6443 \
  --wait \
  --cluster-name "ocm-cluster1" \
  --context "${CTX_MANAGED_CLUSTER}"

# Accept managed cluster
clusteradm accept \
  --clusters ocm-cluster1 \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Verify managed cluster
kubectl get managedcluster ocm-cluster1 -o wide \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Install governance framework on hub
clusteradm install hub-addon \
  --names governance-policy-framework \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Enable governance framework
clusteradm addon enable \
  --names governance-policy-framework \
  --clusters ocm-cluster1 \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Enable config policy controller
clusteradm addon enable \
  --names config-policy-controller \
  --clusters ocm-cluster1 \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Verify addons
kubectl get managedclusteraddon \
  -n ocm-cluster1 \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Verify managed-cluster OCM agents
kubectl get pods \
  -n open-cluster-management-agent \
  --context "${CTX_MANAGED_CLUSTER}"

# Verify policy addons
kubectl get pods \
  -n open-cluster-management-agent-addon \
  --context "${CTX_MANAGED_CLUSTER}"

# Verify ManifestWorks
kubectl get manifestwork \
  -n ocm-cluster1 \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"

# Verify OCM policies
kubectl get policies.policy.open-cluster-management.io -A \
  --context "${CTX_HUB_CLUSTER}"
```

## Success Criteria

The OCM environment is considered healthy when all of the following are true:

```text
ManagedCluster:
    HUB ACCEPTED = true
    JOINED        = True
    AVAILABLE     = True

ManagedClusterAddOns:
    governance-policy-framework = True
    config-policy-controller    = True

Managed cluster pods:
    klusterlet-registration-agent = Running
    klusterlet-work-agent         = Running
    governance-policy-framework   = Running
    config-policy-controller      = Running

Policy:
    Root policy       = Compliant
    Replicated policy = Compliant

ManifestWork:
    Present and successfully applied
```
